{%- comment -%}
  Product card — image, name, price, and a quick-add control.

  Shared by the collection grid, search results, and product recommendations,
  so every product tile on the site is this one file.

  The quick-add "+" is the part that needs care. The prototype draws it as an
  add-to-cart on every card, but this catalog cannot support that: a wig has
  Length, Cap Size and Part, and one product carries 90 variants. There is no
  honest way to pick one on the buyer's behalf, and silently adding the wrong
  size is worse than an extra click.

  So the control is add-to-cart only where that is unambiguous — a purchasable
  product with exactly one variant, which is most Accessories. Everywhere else
  the same button is a link to the product page. It looks identical either way;
  only its accessible name differs, so screen reader users are told which they
  are getting.

  Accepts:
    product          (required)
    loading          'lazy' (default) or 'eager' for above-the-fold cards
    sizes            optional sizes attribute; sensible grid default otherwise
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 1180px) 24vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 92vw'
  assign card_loading = loading | default: 'lazy'

  assign single_variant = false
  if product.variants.size == 1 and product.available
    assign single_variant = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="ness-card">
  <a class="ness-card__media" href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- if product.featured_image -%}
      {{
        product.featured_image
        | image_url: width: 900
        | image_tag:
          class: 'ness-card__image',
          alt: '',
          widths: '260, 390, 520, 780, 900',
          sizes: card_sizes,
          loading: card_loading
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'ness-card__image ness-card__image--placeholder' }}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Sold-out is stated on the card rather than left to the buyer to discover
      on the product page. Pre-order products are legitimately unavailable-but-
      buyable, so this keys off `available`, not inventory.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless product.available -%}
      <span class="ness-card__badge">Sold out</span>
    {%- endunless -%}
  </a>

  <div class="ness-card__foot">
    <div class="ness-card__text">
      {%- comment -%}
        The whole card is reachable from this one link — the media above is
        aria-hidden and untabbable, so the product appears once in the tab
        order and once in a screen reader's link list, not three times.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a class="ness-card__title" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
      <span class="ness-card__price">
        {%- if product.price_varies -%}
          From {{ product.price_min | money }}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ product.price | money }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </div>

    {%- if single_variant -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        data-ness-add is the theme-wide contract with the cart drawer: any form
        carrying it is intercepted by ness-cart.js, posted to /cart/add.js, and
        followed by the drawer opening. Without that script the form submits
        natively and Shopify redirects to /cart.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- form 'product', product, class: 'ness-card__add-form', id: null, data-ness-add: 'true' -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
        <button
          type="submit"
          class="ness-card__add"
          name="add"
          aria-label="Add {{ product.title | escape }} to cart"
        >
          {%- render 'ness-card-plus' -%}
        </button>
      {%- endform -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <a
        class="ness-card__add"
        href="{{ product.url }}"
        aria-label="Choose options for {{ product.title | escape }}"
      >
        {%- render 'ness-card-plus' -%}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
